From: Scott Jones <scottajones@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:24:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06/13] pmdomain: apple: pmp-report: keep the T8122 14.x GPU
 readiness for the M3 runtime

The 7.2 rebase replaced the T8122 14.x branch of
apple_pmp_report_wait_supplier_ready() with a T6030-only one, so on an M3
MacBook Air every GPU power vote returns -ENODEV even with the PMP
running. With the new hidden APPLE_T8122_GPU_PMP_LINK, which
DRM_ASAHI_M3_T8122 selects (as DRM_ASAHI_G15 selects
APPLE_T6030_GPU_PMP_LINK), wait for the unique T8122 report's display
request (DISP, reg 7) to be ready and acknowledged before AGX, as on the
7.1.12 kernel the runtime was qualified with.

The PMP graph and supplier host tests copy the dispatch, so they copy the
T8122 wait too, built off there; their mutations still target the T6030
path.

